    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d822">

                <pb facs="0716" n="706" xml:id="pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/8–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of state </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-11T12:00:00+08:00">August 11,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:05 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 893. Military situation deteriorating so rapidly we may be compelled leave
                    Canton prior August 15.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d822-f1"/> Suggest therefore
                    desirability expediting decision posed Cantel 883, August 5<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d822-f2"/> re closing Canton Consulate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d822-f1" n="66" xml:id="d822-f1-content">
                <p>In telCan No. 553, August 12, <ref target="#pg1313">p. 1313</ref>, the Department
                    authorized closing the Embassy office “whenever in your judgment this move
                    desirable”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d822-f2" n="67" xml:id="d822-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Post</hi>, <ref target="#pg1308">p. 1308</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
